<title>USA: McKesson buys General Medical.</title>
<headline>McKesson buys General Medical.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>McKesson Corp said it signed a definitive agreement to buy General Medical Inc, a privately-held supplier of medical products.</p>
<p>McKesson said it will pay about $775 million for General Medical, including $347 million for the equity, half in McKesson common stock and half in cash, and the assumption of $428 million of debt.</p>
<p>It said that since 1991, General Medical sales have grown at an annual compound rate of about 20 percent, reaching $1.7 billion in 1996.</p>
</text>
